      "id": 8847,
      "name": "Hummingbird",
      "username": "Hummingbird",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/59ef9b/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-10-15T16:42:20.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm using this example that can potentially explain countless other examples.</p><p>It's the villain Omnitron's end of turn on Rampaging Robot side. It has one S-84 Automaton Drone in play which deals X (current HP of itself, for example let's say this one has only 1 HP) energy damage to the highest HP hero at the end of the villain turn, but Omnitron plays the top card of the villain deck at the end of the turn.</p><p>Which one do I resolve first? The S-84 Automaton Drone dealing damage to my highest HP hero or drawing the top card of the villain deck? The card drawn from Rampaging Robot's end of turn ability could be another S-84 Automaton Drone (this time with full HP), therefore doing more damage to my highest HP hero. Which one I resolve first could change the outcome of who gets damaged and by how much.</p><p>Thanks for helping.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:28.633Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
