    {
      "id": 77260,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-10-15T17:09:43.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Yeah, with end of turn or start of turn effects they go by the order the cards came into play.</p><p>The best guide we have right now is:</p><p>If a single event would cause multiple card effects to activate, they activate in the order they entered play, if multiple effects on one card activate, do them in the order on the card.</p><p>If a single card effect causes multiple things to happen (Destroy a bunch of cards, everyone draw a card or deal multiple targets damage) the players decide the order it happens in.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:58:12.857Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
