      "username": "dpt",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-10-15T18:44:22.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><b>Foote wrote:</b></p>\n<div><blockquote>All at once</blockquote></div>\nand by all at once he means in the order the heroes choose, but all destroyed once 7 damage is reached. \n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I doubt it would ever matter, but I think the components would actually be destroyed in the order they came into play. There is a triggering event (dealing at least 7 damage), and the cards respond to that event in the usual order, which is as the cards were played.</p>",
