      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-10-15T18:48:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>phantaskippy wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Foote wrote:<br><blockquote>All at once\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nand by all at once he means in the order the heroes choose, but all destroyed once 7 damage is reached.\n</blockquote></div>\nI doubt it would ever matter, but I think the components would actually be destroyed in the order they came into play. There is a triggering event (dealing at least 7 damage), and the cards respond to that event in the usual order, which is as the cards were played.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>At that point it's kinda&nbsp;a \"6 of one, half dozen of the other\" sort of thing. But technically you are correct. They would get destroyed in order. Why? Because they are simultaneaous triggers! And we have come full circle.</p>",
