      "id": 77267,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-10-15T21:35:30.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I doubt it would ever matter, but I think the components would actually be destroyed in the order they came into play. There is a triggering event (dealing at least 7 damage), and the cards respond to that event in the usual order, which is as the cards were played.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I don't have Omnitron's deck in front of me. If you're playing in the Realm of Discord and Imbued Vitality is out, such that the components are targets, such that Chronoranger could put bounties on them, are there any components that would have an effect based on Chronoranger doing something, like drawing a card?</p>",
